  "limits": [
    "This is not physical DMA execution or a FreeRTOS scheduler. Synthetic DMA overwrites are an explicit input, not an observed dropout.",
    "Queued pointers and borrowed-buffer lifetime are proven for the recovered producer/reader; exact wall-clock reuse and interrupt latency are not.",
    "The ring allocation failure stops at the attempted address-zero store. It does not execute an ESP32 exception handler or establish a reset on the owned frames.",
